[center][size=6][b]MCRN Corvette[/b][/size]
[size=4]The Tachi / Rocinante: A Corvette-class light frigate from [i]The Expanse[/i][/size]
[size=3]A legitimate salvage for Hardspace: Shipbreaker · v0.9.12[/size][/center]

[line]

This a full-size warship to cut apart, deck by deck. It is built as a tower, the way the ship flies in the show: engine at the bottom, flight deck at the top, and twelve walkable decks stacked between them.

It is about three times the size of the exterior ship on screen, to match the approximate size of the interior scenes.  Watch those doors and corners!

[center][img width=402]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/KerballOne/ShipbreakerShipbuilder/master/Assets/_CustomShips/Tachi/Textures/TachiShipCatalog.png[/img][img width=387]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/KerballOne/ShipbreakerShipbuilder/master/Assets/_CustomShips/Tachi/Textures/TachiShipCatalog_Rocinante.png[/img]

[img width=602]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/KerballOne/ShipbreakerShipbuilder/master/Assets/_CustomShips/Tachi/Textures/TachiShipCatalog_Gas.png[/img][/center]

[size=5][b]Three ships in one download[/b][/size]
Free Play and the Career job board list three ships, each with its own name and picture:
[list]
[*][b]MCRN Tachi.[/b] The corvette in Martian navy colors, with all six point defense cannons, a full crew's bunks and MCRN posters on the walls.
[*][b]Rocinante.[/b] The same ship after she left the Martian navy: an independent warship in her own colors. Belter posters on the walls, one bunk per cabin and a galley with fewer tables, for a much smaller crew.
[*][b]Beratnas Gas Hauler.[/b] The same hull stripped of its cannons and carrying 24 gas tanks on external racks: 16 large and 8 small. The racks hang on the hull by cut points alone. She is too wide to sit between the bay's light jacks, so she is parked level above them. Inside she matches the Rocinante: Belter posters, one bunk per cabin, fewer galley tables.
[/list]


[size=5][b]What's aboard[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]12 decks.[/b] Engineering, weapons storage and control, galley, crew cabins, medbay, cargo holds, airlocks, command deck and flight deck.
[*][b]6 point defense cannons[/b], each with its ammunition belt and crates (MCRN Tachi and Rocinante).
[*][b]2 torpedo tubes and 12 torpedoes.[/b] Handle with care: they are worth salvaging and they explode.
[*][b]Keel railgun (Rocinante only).[/b] Loaded through the Weapons Control wall from a crate of 20 slugs. Two generators sit on its breech: pull the breakers before you take them off.
[*][b]Fusion reactor and main drive.[/b] Eight plasma injectors feed the Solomon Epstein Drive.
[*][b]A full utility crawlspace[/b] carrying the power, coolant, fuel and ammunition runs between decks, with two generators on the tunnel roof and backup power cells beside the torpedo tubes.
[*][b]Free Play and Career.[/b] All three ships are in the Free Play list and can appear on the Career job board.
[*][b]28 crew bunks, 5 medbay beds and 32 acceleration couches.[/b] The Rocinante and the Gas Hauler have 12 crew bunks.
[*][b]Loose salvage.[/b] Bottles, snacks, credit and data drives, oxygen and thruster fuel, suit pieces and spare parts.
[*][b]One body.[/b] A dead spacer floats somewhere aboard, in one of six places. Who it was changes from ship to ship: seven factions, each with its own suit colors and visor.
[*][b]Ghost ships.[/b] Taken as a ghost ship, any of the three is overgrown: dozens of Protomolecule nodes to destroy, several on every deck, and blue growth across the hull, walls, floors and ceilings. A normal ship has none of it.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Numbers[/b][/size]
The MCRN Tachi and the Rocinante are the same ship in different colors and share these figures. The Gas Hauler's are in brackets.
[list]
[*][b]Length:[/b] 133.7 m
[*][b]Beam:[/b] 54.6 m (Gas Hauler: 67.2 m)
[*][b]Height:[/b] 46.3 m (Gas Hauler: 55.1 m)
[*][b]Parts:[/b] 5,311, Rocinante 5,215 (Gas Hauler: 5,736); and more as a ghost ship
[*][b]Cut points:[/b] 260 (Gas Hauler: 343)
[*][b]Estimated mass:[/b] at least 268 t (Gas Hauler: about 394 t)
[*][b]Gas tanks:[/b] large about 7.5 t each, small about 5.5 t each
[*][b]Download:[/b] 198 MB for all three ships
[/list]

